YAML
Yaml aint markup language. Its a data serilization language. 
What is data serilization language?
If application are developed in different technology, to transfer data between then they will use data serilization language. Most famous data serilization languages are JSON, XML and YAML.
Yaml mainly used to create a configuration file for devops tools like docker, kubernites, ansible , prometheus etc and it will be save in .yaml or .yml .Here Yaml is humal redablle format and here it will written like line seperation and indentation. if we miss thease 2 we will get error.
YAML Syntax:
Below will be used while creating yaml configuration file
Key-value pair
Comments
Objects
Boolen
List
multilineString
singlelineString
env variable
placeholder

Example below:
Key-value pair - Onvalue we no need to metion " or ' for string , by default yaml will differentiate. if we add special character in value need to enclose the string with " or '
appname: qTest-backend
Comments:
# app name
appname: qTest-backend
Object - Adding group of values together or use group of values together. Here microservices is object and appname, version and port are values. Need to use indentation and new line for each value
microservices:
  appname: qTest-backend
  version: 1.0
  port: 5001
Boolen - Here can use true or false, yes or no and on or off as boolen. Here deployed we used boolen datatype
microservices:
  appname: qTest-backend
  version: 1.0
  port: 5001
  deployed: false
List - We can create list as well in yaml. It should differentiate with - .Here microservices is list variable inside that we have 2 list ie which start with -
microservices:
  - appname: qTest-backend
    version: 1.0
    port: 5001
    deployed: false
  - appname: java-backend
    version: 1.0
    port: 5002
    deployed: true
Can define list with name alone like this. Here microserviceslist have 3 values.
microservices:
  - qtest
  - jira
  - github
We can define like below as well ie version has 3 values 1.0, 2.0 and 3.0 else like this as well ["1.0", 2.0, 3.0]. Both same here i just made one as string in the list
microservices:
  - appname: qTest-backend
    version: ["1.0", 2.0, 3.0]
    port: 5001
    deployed: false
  - appname: java-backend
    version:
      - 1.0
      - 2.0
      - 3.o
    port: 5002
    deployed: true
Can validate yaml file using online validator as well before deploying into devops applications.
multilineString - for a key if we need to define a multiline string can be define using | . So here appname interrept the below line as multi line string
appName: |
  this is my first tutorial on yaml
  I gained knowledge with this course
  It really helps

singlelineString - for a key if we need to define a singleline string can be define using > . So here appname interrept the below line as single line string
appName: >
  this is my first tutorial on yaml
  I gained knowledge with this course
  It really helps

env variable - if we need to access the env variable in yaml need to call using $. eg $port
placeholder - if we have placeholder in different place and need to call in yaml need to call using {{}} - inside {{}} we will give the key value which get from placeholder in someplace. Passing the variable is placeholder
appName: {{ .Value.service.name}}

multiple yaml document - to add the multiple component in single yaml file we use --- eg two different configuration in one yaml file
Eg below

microservices:
  - appname: qTest-backend
    version: ["1.0", 2.0, 3.0]
    port: 5001
    deployed: false
  - appname: java-backend
    version:
      - 1.0
      - 2.0
      - 3.o
    port: 5002
    deployed: true
